---
description: Launch the app this branch actually builds, as soon as code changes are done
alwaysApply: true
---

After finishing code changes in this repo, launch the new build before ending the turn, then close
it again so no window or process is left behind.

**Editing `zr/apps/zgx/ui/**` (Luau) needs no rebuild.** Screens, the design system and plugins are
read from disk and reload as they are saved. Only Rust changes (`zr/crates/**`,
`zr/apps/zgx/src/**`) need the build below.

`cargo run -p dove` cannot work: `apps/dove` is excluded from the root workspace, so there is no
`dove` package. The launchable app is `zr/apps/zgx`, a workspace of its own, and it needs
`keplorayx-engine.exe` beside it:

```sh
# 1. the app (keplorayx.exe)
cd zr/apps/zgx && cargo build --locked

# 2. the engine it starts (keplorayx-engine.exe)
cd ../.. && cargo build --locked -p zeron --bin keplorayx-engine

# 3. the app looks for the engine beside itself
cp target/debug/keplorayx-engine.exe apps/zgx/target/debug/

# 4. run it
apps/zgx/target/debug/keplorayx.exe main
```

Keep `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` outside the checkout if you do not want `target/` in the working copy, and
pass the **same** value to both builds so step 3 copies from the right place. Other entry points:
`keplorayx.exe` alone (intro, then setup), `--background` (tray and notch, window hidden),
`launcher`, `notch`, `onboarding`, `gallery`.

Before starting, close any `keplorayx.exe` already running from this checkout so the window the user
sees is the new build; only one process can own the global keys. Kill it again when the check is
done.
